PERKS WEBSITE PACKAGE

FILES
- index.html: Home page with five-slide hero carousel.
- services.html: Appointment booking form.
- quotation.html: Select services, calculate total, print/save PDF, send quotation.
- style.css: Shared responsive black-and-gold styling.
- script.js: Carousel, form logic, EmailJS and WhatsApp settings.
- assets/perks-logo.png: Uploaded PERKS logo.

ADD YOUR FIVE SLIDER IMAGES
Create an "images" folder beside index.html and add:
sports-car-1.jpg
sports-car-2.jpg
sports-car-3.jpg
sports-car-4.jpg
sports-car-5.jpg
The slider already points to these names.

IMPORTANT SETUP BEFORE GOING LIVE
1. Open script.js and replace:
   companyEmail with the actual company email.
   whatsappNumber with the business WhatsApp number including country code, digits only.
2. Email delivery needs EmailJS configuration:
   - Create an EmailJS account at https://www.emailjs.com/
   - Add an email service connected to your company mailbox.
   - Create two templates: one for appointment requests and one for quotation requests.
   - Add the Public Key, Service ID, Booking Template ID and Quotation Template ID in script.js.
   - In each template, use the variables: {{to_email}}, {{reference}}, {{name}}, {{phone}}, {{email}}, {{vehicle}}, {{service}}, {{date}}, {{time}}, {{services}}, {{total}}, {{message}}, {{notes}}.
   The template can include the variables relevant to that form. Set the recipient to the dynamic {{to_email}} field.
3. Replace the sample quotation prices in quotation.html with approved PERKS prices (AED is currently used as the display currency).
4. Replace the sample WhatsApp link in the header (971XXXXXXXXX) in all three HTML files with the real WhatsApp number.
5. Upload the full folder to your hosting provider / GitHub Pages.

NOTES
- The booking form is a request, not a confirmed appointment. PERKS must confirm availability.
- EmailJS is a third-party email service. Configure and test it before publishing.
- The quotation form opens WhatsApp with a prepared message; the customer must press Send in WhatsApp.
- This starter is a front-end website. It does not yet include a secure admin dashboard or a database of bookings.
- The provided image reference is used for the logo. Hero sports-car images are intentionally left as replaceable image slots.
